      "raw": "In each of the three views, the same three garments are present: a pair of black cargo pants, a red-and-white striped t-shirt, and a pair of gray shorts. The regions provided in each view correspond to these garments, and the same garments appear in every view, even though their positions shift.\n\n- In **VIEW control_07_all_present_v0**, the regions are:\n  - R001: black cargo pants\n  - R002: red-and-white striped t-shirt\n  - R003: gray shorts\n\n- In **VIEW control_07_all_present_v1**, the regions are:\n  - R004: black cargo pants (same as R001)\n  - R005: red-and-white striped t-shirt (same as R002)\n  - R006: gray shorts (same as R003)\n\n- In **VIEW control_07_all_present_v2**, the regions are:\n  - R007: black cargo pants (same as R001 and R004)\n  - R008: red-and-white striped t-shirt (same as R002 and R005)\n  - R009: gray shorts (same as R003 and R006)\n\nEach garment is consistently represented across all views with unique region IDs per view, and no garment is missing from any view. The garments are visually distinct by fabric, color, and construction, and there is no ambiguity in matching them across views.\n\nThus, we assign each garment to a track using the region IDs from each view.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"tracks\": [\n    {\n      \"garment\": \"black cargo pants\",\n      \"regions\": [\"R001\", \"R004\", \"R007\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"garment\": \"red-and-white striped t-shirt\",\n      \"regions\": [\"R002\", \"R005\", \"R008\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"garment\": \"gray shorts\",\n      \"regions\": [\"R003\", \"R006\", \"R009\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
